note='''Notes on printed music-staff paper, upright, manuscript foot number 341. The page compares chains/cochains of the standard simplex with exterior powers, represents evaluation by Hom from the free simplicial module, and contrasts exterior and interior product structures. The two exterior-power Hom rows reverse the written m,n arguments but both right-side complexes bear [n]; the first equality therefore remains as written rather than being repaired to H’s [m]. The chosen lambda has exponent 1+i although its complex degree is a bullet. The isolated dot in the second upper row is retained, not promoted to equals by the printed ruling. The lower note says “pas linéaire !”; the tall initial p is not an arrow. Both dual trial expressions are cancelled. No general equivalence claimed in this working page has been proved here. The elementary representable evaluation identity was checked directly: a simplicial map from the representable simplex is determined by the image of its identity n-simplex; extension to the free k-module gives the displayed k-linear version. This does not validate the page’s other exterior-power identifications or reverse its explicit indices.'''
commit(n,text,ds,cs,inventory,note,hand=['The printed horizontal staves must not be counted as equality strokes: the blue dot in the second row is separate; H supplies an equals.','The tall initial p in pas has a deep narrow loop; C mistook it for an upward double arrow. This observation is local, not a rule for every tall stroke.','Vertical paired ticks again express equality (above the dual identity and between Hom rows), consistent with scan 339.'],notation=[(r'\Vert','Two parallel upright strokes between displayed rows, a rotated equality.'),(r'\mathbb C_* , C_\bullet','Doubled C in the simplicial/free identities is distinguished from the single C of the exterior-power complex.'),(r'\text{prod. ext / prod. int}','Different product labels; the lower one is interior, not exterior.')],abbr=[('prod. ext','produit extérieur'),('prod. int','produit intérieur')],checks=[check('340-representable-evaluation','A map from Delta^n_* is determined by the image of its identity n-simplex; the naturality equations reconstruct its other components. Extending basis elements linearly gives Hom_k(k[Delta^n_*],lambda_*)=lambda_[n].','targeted proof check'),check('340-exterior-identifications','Recorded as manuscript assertions only; the inconsistent argument order and index are retained, not proved.')],unresolved=[r'cancelled a/alpha in the first row',r'cancelled Phi before lambda remains tentative'])
